<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sho Shisho</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1421</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Shō Shishō</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sho Shisho was king of Chuzan on Okinawa from 1407 to 1421 and the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-sho-dynasty">First Sho dynasty</a>. In 1406 he and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sho-hashi">Sho Hashi</a> overthrew King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bunei">Bunei</a> and moved the capital to Shuri. He received recognition from Ming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> as king, while his son led the campaigns that soon united Okinawa as the Ryukyu Kingdom.</p></div>
